{:policy-pack/system
 {;; Signature verification outcomes (N4 §8.2) and trust-root config
  ;; diagnostics (§8.2.1). Operator-facing: they explain why a pack was
  ;; refused or why a trust root would not load, and they reach logs and
  ;; evidence rather than a product surface, so they live in the system
  ;; locale.
  :verify/unsigned
  "Pack is not signed"

  :verify/missing-key-id
  "Pack carries a signature but no :pack/signed-by key identifier"

  :verify/untrusted-key-id
  "Pack signer is not in the configured trust roots"

  :crypto/bad-public-key-length
  "Trusted public key is not a 32-byte raw Ed25519 key"

  :crypto/undecodable-signature
  "Pack signature is not a readable base64 string"

  :crypto/invalid-signature
  "Pack signature does not verify against the trusted public key"

  :crypto/verification-error
  "Ed25519 verification failed without an error message"

  :trust-roots/invalid-public-key
  "must be base64 of a raw {bytes}-byte Ed25519 public key"

  :trust-roots/invalid-entry
  "Invalid policy pack trust root: {key-id}"

  :trust-roots/invalid-config
  "Invalid policy pack trust-root config: {source}"

  ;; MDC compile diagnostics. Developer-facing: they reach the output of
  ;; `bb standards:pack` and the pack's :warnings, not a product surface.
  :mdc/nested-block-frontmatter
  "{filename}: frontmatter key '{key}' is a nested YAML block, which the MDC grammar cannot represent — its indented children parsed as separate top-level keys, so '{key}.*' resolved to nothing and the rule compiled with detection {detection} and enforcement {action}. Rewrite as dotted keys: '{key}.<child>: <value>'."

  :mdc/nested-block-compile-failed
  "{filename}: frontmatter key '{key}' is a nested YAML block, which the MDC grammar cannot represent. The compile error reported for this file is a symptom of it — an indented dotted child collides with the parent key during grouping. Rewrite as dotted keys: '{key}.<child>: <value>'."

  :mdc/commented-list-value
  "{filename}: frontmatter key '{key}' has a comment as its only value, so the '- item' list written under it was discarded and the key compiled as the comment text ({value}). Put the comment on its own line above the key."

  :mdc/interrupted-list
  "{filename}: a comment containing a colon sits inside the '- item' list under frontmatter key '{key}', so the parser read it as a key and dropped the list items after it — the key compiled as {value}. Remove the colon from the comment, or move the comment above the key."

  :mdc/compile-failed
  "Failed to compile {filename}: {error}"

  :mdc/always-inject-no-phases
  "Some always-inject rules have no applicable phases (Dewey 900 meta range)"}}
